+---
+id: task-005-create-json-patch-from-two-documents-createpatch
+type: task
+title: "Create JSON Patch from two documents (createPatch)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. Export
+`createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`, returning a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from` into `to`,
+without mutating either input. The patch must describe only what changed; an array item added or removed is
+an `add`/`remove`, and a moved item is a `move` or `remove` + `add`, without rewriting the items around it.
+
+# What was done
+
+- `createPatch` in `src/index.ts`: objects are diffed member by member (`remove`, `add`, recursion); differing
+  primitives or types give `replace` (path `""` for the root). Arrays: common prefix and suffix are trimmed, then
+  a longest common subsequence keeps shared items; gaps are paired for in-place recursive diffs, the rest become
+  `add`/`remove`. A moved item is therefore a `remove` and an `add`.
+- Pointer tokens are escaped per RFC 6901 section 3; values in the patch are deep copies (no shared structure);
+  keys are read as own members only, so `__proto__` is safe.
+- Tests in `test/create-patch.test.ts`: minimality cases, escaping, type changes, array insert/remove/move,
+  non-mutation, prototype safety, and 2000 randomised round trips through `applyPatch`. `npm test`: 100 pass, 0 fail.
+- `README.md` documents the new function.
